 3 neighbors survives\n- Rule 3 (Overpopulation): center cell with 4 neighbors dies \n- Rule 4 (Reproduction): dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors becomes alive\n- Blinker (oscillator): vertical to horizontal and back\n- Block (still life): unchanged\n- Single cell dies\n\nLet me order from simplest to most complex and create the test file:\n\nSimplest → most complex:\n1. Empty grid → empty grid\n2. Single cell dies (simplest non-empty case)\n3. Underpopulation: two adjacent cells die\n4. Survival: cell with 2 neighbors lives\n5. Survival: cell with 3 neighbors lives\n6. Overpopulation: cell with >3 neighbors dies\n7. Reproduction: dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors becomes alive\n8. Block (still life): 2x2 block unchanged\n9. Blinker (oscillator): period 2\n\nNow create the test file:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_36c8686654c140c0b4afc1d9","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_12-09-16_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/game-of-life.spec.ts","content":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { nextGeneration } from \"./game-of-life.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Game of Life - Next Generation\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"should return empty grid for empty input -- [] → []\");\n  it.todo(\"should kill a single lone cell -- [(0,0)] → []\");\n  it.todo(\"should kill live cells with fewer than 2 neighbors (underpopulation) -- [(0,1), (1,1)] → []\");\n  it.todo(\"should keep a live cell with exactly 2 neighbors alive (survival)\");\n  it.todo(\"should keep a live cell with exactly 3 neighbors alive (survival)\");\n  it.todo(\"should kill a live cell with more than 3 neighbors (overpopulation) -- center cell (1,1) with 4 neighbors dies\");\n  it.todo(\"should bring dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors to life (reproduction) -- dead cell (1,1) with 3 neighbors becomes alive\");\n  it.todo(\"should preserve a 2×2 block unchanged (still life) -- [(0,0),(1,0),(0,1),(1,1)] → same\");\n  it.todo(\"should oscillate a blinker (period 2 oscillator) -- vertical [(0,0),(0,1),(0,2)] → horizontal [(-1,1),(0,1),(1,1)]\");\n});"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":2921,"output":749,"cacheRead":8448,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12118,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784981365760,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-35e3dd47-598d-4bdf-94d6-9731d4b65ad1","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_36c8686654c140c0b4afc1d9","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1037 bytes to /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_12-09-16_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/game-of-life.spec.ts"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784981370862},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Test List\n\n**Feature**: Game of Life - Next Generation (infinite grid, sparse representation)\n**Test File**: `src/game-of-life.spec.ts`\n**Tests**: 9\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple → complex):\n1. should return empty grid for empty input -- [] → []\n2. should kill a single lone cell -- [(0,0)] → []\n3. should kill live cells with fewer than 2 neighbors (underpopulation) -- [(0,1), (1,1)] → []\n4. should keep a live cell with exactly 2 neighbors alive (survival)\n5. should keep a live cell with exactly 3 neighbors alive (survival)\n6. should kill a live cell with more than 3 neighbors (overpopulation) -- center cell (1,1) with 4 neighbors dies\n7. should bring dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors to life (reproduction) -- dead cell (1,1) with 3 neighbors becomes alive\n8. should preserve a 2×2 block unchanged (still life) -- [(0,0),(1,0),(0,1),(1,1)] → same\n9. should oscillate a blinker (period 2 oscillator) -- vertical [(0,0),(0,1),(0,2)] → horizontal [(-1,1),(0,1),(1,1)]\n\n**Coverage**: All 4 rules (underpopulation, s